ministers meeting at the General Affairs  Council prepared work ahead of the march  EU summit which main focus will be to  promote the creation of an energy union  the aim is to make the EU market more  competitive more sustainable and to  ensure security of supply I believe that  European Council later this week will be  able to agree on some pillars creating  energy union that's security solidarity  also development of internal energy  market efficiency the carburizing  decarbonizing of energy sources and  development of research the council has  also examined external relations issues  they include preparations for the next  Eastern Partnership summit in Riga as  well as relations with Russia and the  situation in Ukraine and Libya the  European economy was also on the agenda  ministers have discussed the European  fund for strategic investment and ways  that it can contribute to growth and  jobs in the EU moreover the council made  preparations for the first phase of the  European semester 4 2015 where Member  States agree on economic and fiscal  policy priorities for a given year
 

